+ * t5dr offline soak (patch 0041): blocks are reused. This was a bump
+ * allocator that never freed, on the theory that titles create their threads
+ * at boot and keep them. Tekken 5 DR does not: with its 64 KB TLS segment
+ * (0x18000 per block) the 1 MB window holds 9 blocks, it creates 11 threads at
+ * boot and then a thread per sound stream and movie, about 380 an hour. So
+ * from the boot on, and for every thread after that, the "out of room" path
+ * ran and those threads all shared one block -- the loader's first image,
+ * which nobody owns once the CRT's sys_initialize_tls has moved the main
+ * thread elsewhere. Whatever the title keeps per thread (errno, its allocator
+ * context) was shared between them.
